A||N||3||superXmotorsports||low oil pressure||||5||
Z||000000||superXmotorsports||01-24-2000||10:32 PM||||The oil pressure in my 87 GT is very low at idle when the engine is warm that the oil light comes on.  The pressure is good when it's above 1500RPM's though.  Any thoughts?  Thanks.  SXM.||||reg||5
Z||000001||superXmotorsports||01-24-2000||10:35 PM||||Sorry about the double - answer to either one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Actually if someone has the authority delete the other.  Thanks!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||01-24-2000||10:52 PM||||Oil pressure is regulated by a relief spring that bypasses the oil at a preset level, since the pressure comes up at 1500 the spring is working.  Not enough volume at low rpms.  The design of these engines flows the oil through the lifter galleries on the way to the bearings.  If the engine does not rattle its bearings on startup then the pressure is probably bleeding off through the lifters or around the lifters.  If it gives a good rattle when started, maybe too much clearance worn into the bearings. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierospeeder||01-25-2000||08:39 PM||||I bought my car with the oil light going on.  First check if the oil pan was dented.  The other thing was my changing my oilpump and that fixed it.  You can try using thicker oil like 10w40, and if that works, that might mean your bearings are going bad.||||reg||1
